    "payload": "tree 59a0927fa2b1e7b6a7043bbc8f7614bd2dde7f05\nparent 27d7bd860ee903fac20cc6ad187535110a8cd198\nauthor Arhan Canli <arhancanli8@gmail.com> 1791001823 +0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791001823 +0400\n\nfix: preserve standards skip-link focus through build\n\nThe standards page committed a skip link without the shared `skip-link` class and a `main#content` without `tabindex=\"-1\"`. Align that mirror with the generator and verify both source and built output at the end of postbuild, so those attributes cannot drift silently.\n\nThe bounded guard uses strict UTF-8 and a stable file descriptor. Ignored comment/script/style spans retain their width, preventing surrounding text from becoming a fabricated tag. Nine meaningful cases cover the original missing attributes, duplicate targets/controls, ignored spans, malformed or oversized input, and the standards page's focusable target.\n\nValidation on final signed `988381a54e4e73e598507685b575b4f17ef4250e`: all seven checks pass; all nine cases pass once in ROOT, with suites 6 + 1117 + 9 and MCP suites 141 + 1 + 82 + 119 + 139 on Node 22.23.3. The source and dist guards each pass once. Tested merge `11a009d30fdb5e5add5195b93d98a4c85fe73f37` has the exact candidate tree. The captured current-ref CodeQL alert list is empty and both latest language analyses report zero results.\n\n[The 40-file evidence manifest](https://github.com/arhancanli/canlicapital/blob/988381a54e4e73e598507685b575b4f17ef4250e/docs/goal/evidence/standard-skip-focus-20261003/manifest.json) preserves the original CodeQL 91 finding, correction, raw CI and independent source/CI reviews. Code snapshots are exact text artifacts. Final-head review receipts stay outside that frozen archive.\n\nThe cause of the earlier live attribute loss remains unproven. This verifies template/build behavior; production publication and browser focus verification remain separate. No generator, server, schema, data, journal, dependency, lock, version or unrelated product change.",
